    "content": "  Structural basis of AAV liver de-targeting and neuronal tropism - CLOVER Center                                  \n\n[skip to main content](#content)\n\n[![Caltech](/static/core/img/caltech-new-logo.png)](https://www.caltech.edu)\n\n[CLOVER Center CLARITY, Optogenetics, & Vector Engineering](/)\n\n-   [AAV Repository](/aav-repository)\n    \n-   [ASPIRE Program](/aspire-program)\n    \n-   [Obtaining Reagents](/reagents)\n    \n-   [People](/People)\n    \n-   [Publications](/Publications)\n    \n-   [Contact](/Contact)\n    \n-   ![](/static/wagtail_menu/img/icon-search.png)\n    \n    SearchSearch\n    \n\nMenu ![](/static/wagtail_menu/img/menu-burger.png) \n\nClose\n\n-   [AAV Repository](/aav-repository)\n-   [ASPIRE Program](/aspire-program)\n-   [Obtaining Reagents](/reagents)\n-   [People](/People)\n-   [Publications](/Publications)\n-   [Contact](/Contact)\n\n![](/static/wagtail_menu/img/icon-search.png)\n\nSearchSearch\n\n[Home](/)  /  [News](/news)  /  Structural basis of AAV liver de-targeting and neuronal tropism\n\n![ebrte](https://caltechsites-prod-assets.resources.caltech.edu/clover/images/Screen_Shot_2026-03-30_at_1..234eb12a.fill-1600x810-c100.jpg)\n\n# Structural basis of AAV liver de-targeting and neuronal tropism\n\nMarch 30, 2026\n\nCLOVER-affiliated graduate student Tyler Brittain and Postdoctoral Fellow Seongmin Jang led a team effort to determine the structural basis of AAV tropism modulation away from liver and non-neuronal CNS cells using cryo-EM, biophysical assays, and in vivo characterization of [CAP-B10](/news/new-aav-for-mice-and-marmosets-that-are-enhanced-in-cns-decreased-in-liver), [AAV9-X1.1](/news/new-capsids-for-mouse-brain-endothelium-and-nhp-brain-neurons), and other capsids. Coauthors include current and former CLOVER staff Izabela Giriat, Fiona Ristic, and Tim Shay.\n\n#### Check out the full story at [Molecular Therapy](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ymthe.2026.03.030), where it was featured on the cover of the [July issue](https://www.cell.com/molecular-therapy/current#), and discussed in a [commentary highlighting the work](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ymthe.2026.06.024).\n\n#### Congrats to Tyler, Seongmin, and the team!\n\n ![](https://caltechsites-prod-assets.resources.caltech.edu/clover/images/Jang_cover.tif.7d84b51b.width-450.jpg)![erbet](https://caltechsites-prod-assets.resources.caltech.edu/clover/images/Screen_Shot_2026-03-30_at_12.20.32_PM.938f442b.width-450.png)\n\n![](https://caltechsites-prod-assets.resources.caltech.edu/clover/images/Jang_cover.tif.f52997df.fill-75x75.jpg)![erbet](https://caltechsites-prod-assets.resources.caltech.edu/clover/images/Screen_Shot_2026-03-30_at_12.20.32_P.5650fd44.fill-75x75.png)\n\nImage Lightbox\n\n![](/static/theme-v7.0/img/flame.png)\n\n![Caltech](/static/core/img/caltech-new-logo.png)\n\nCalifornia Institute of Technology\n\n![](/static/theme-v7.0/img/icon-footerpin.png)\n\n1200 East California Boulevard\n\nPasadena, California 91125\n\n[Digital Accessibility](https://digitalaccessibility.caltech.edu/) | [Privacy Notice](https://www.caltech.edu/privacy-notice) | Site Content Copyright © 2026 | [Log In](https://clover.caltech.edu/admin/login/)"
